{
  "cells": [
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "# Evaluation \u2014 FID, CLIP Score, Human Preference Notebook\n\n> Hands-on Build It and Exercises."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "## Build It"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "`code/main.py` implements FID, CLIP-score-like, and Elo aggregation on synthetic \"feature vectors\" (we use 4-D vectors as stand-ins for Inception features). You see:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "- FID computation on a small N and on a large N \u2014 the bias."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "- \"CLIP score\" as cosine similarity between feature pools."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "- Elo update rule from a synthetic preference stream."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Step 1: FID in four lines"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```python"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "def fid(real_features, gen_features):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    mu_r, cov_r = mean_and_cov(real_features)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    mu_g, cov_g = mean_and_cov(gen_features)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    mean_diff = sum((a - b) ** 2 for a, b in zip(mu_r, mu_g))"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    trace_term = trace(cov_r) + trace(cov_g) - 2 * sqrt_cov_product(cov_r, cov_g)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    return mean_diff + trace_term"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Step 2: CLIP-style cosine-similarity"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```python"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "def clip_like(image_feat, text_feat):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    dot = sum(a * b for a, b in zip(image_feat, text_feat))"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    norm = math.sqrt(dot_self(image_feat) * dot_self(text_feat))"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    return dot / max(norm, 1e-8)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Step 3: Elo aggregation"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```python"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "def elo_update(r_a, r_b, winner, k=32):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    expected_a = 1 / (1 + 10 ** ((r_b - r_a) / 400))"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    actual_a = 1.0 if winner == \"a\" else 0.0"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    r_a_new = r_a + k * (actual_a - expected_a)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    r_b_new = r_b - k * (actual_a - expected_a)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    return r_a_new, r_b_new"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "## Exercises"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "1. **Easy.** Run `code/main.py`. Compare FID at N=100 vs N=1000 on the same synthetic distributions. Report bias magnitude.\n2. **Medium.** Implement CMMD from synthetic CLIP-style features (see Jayasumana et al., 2024 for the formula). Compare sensitivity to quality differences vs FID.\n3. **Hard.** Replicate the HPSv2 setup: take 1000 image-prompt pairs from a subset of Pick-a-Pic, fine-tune a small CLIP-based scorer on the preferences, and measure its agreement with a held-out set."
      ]
    }
